 of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bb8718-31f1-5adc-ae1f-1d7bd30a16c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-46 & 8 \\\\ 20 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327131} {:answer/id #uuid "489edc5a-60be-5dce-86c1-05ab0753cd15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-46 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327566} {:answer/id #uuid "8b22a9b6-cb58-5971-b2f0-0c7c96723f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-46 & -6 \\\\ 20 & 6\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328128} {:answer/id #uuid "b68463fb-3810-554a-b331-1be2223e4970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328521} {:answer/id #uuid "db8d7e2e-fc8d-5493-b546-9ffdef5194e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & -20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b68463fb-3810-554a-b331-1be2223e4970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328521} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7c8d9d-0c88-57e3-9cb0-747cc01be221" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6100a287-68c7-5caf-9d53-cb69062757b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42977" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|},$ \nwhere ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & \\,8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc4cd7d-9eb6-5394-836d-01389afe841f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118803} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f3c696-5951-5f6d-b7ec-9c2fe110ca25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118804} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa72ef2-be17-5172-b51c-f6deb64a9261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118805} {:answer/id #uuid "ec39aa0f-9ae9-5158-b8e1-c1ee129803b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118806} {:answer/id #uuid "53e7ecde-8592-5a56-8a4e-5413b7808c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa72ef2-be17-5172-b51c-f6deb64a9261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118805} :answer-field/id #uuid "591cf863-263f-5798-a041-3edb5ac56202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38525400-a144-5244-a7f9-f068d294beba" :question/math-academy-id "q-42983" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=10 \\\\ kx-4y=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04b6012-a48f-5721-94d7-14a720086239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328462} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e8c928-34ff-5dce-974c-34fd1be690e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328515} {:answer/id #uuid "b7970d03-9ceb-5a0a-8e97-9d811b8d1736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328531} {:answer/id #uuid "d38b81dd-4d64-5985-b859-58fcb61204e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328791} {:answer/id #uuid "eb911ac8-402a-5949-828c-c8971c8b567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb911ac8-402a-5949-828c-c8971c8b567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328995} :answer-field/id #uuid "355316d1-ee71-5d92-a11e-e5f4d5c5172c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "854132a3-b7f0-5d3e-b0d4-55e43fe2b0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-42984" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=k \\\\ 2x-y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-13$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=13$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3-10 \\\\  & -13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|}{-13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)(-13) \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f13ed83-8c4f-597b-9f02-b31307021e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441126} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc8305b-aa26-5938-bd09-82bace4ba090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441128} {:answer/id #uuid "742473cb-daf1-51d3-8173-d6d820c2cd4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441131} {:answer/id #uuid "bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441134} {:answer/id #uuid "f4490cc5-d61d-513b-835c-43fda69e74cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441134} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7f776c-eb99-528b-aabd-b4033c71b940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199" :question/math-academy-id "q-42985" :question/problem "Let $⟨-12,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+9y=42 \\\\ kx+10y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-38$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=456$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}42 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =420+36 \\\\  & =456.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{456}{|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =\\frac{456}{-12} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ea719f-cc5a-529e-b60d-0bfadf8ca55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336072} {:answer/id #uuid "2d83fce9-f1b8-5db4-ab58-7c31474bb04c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336469} {:answer/id #uuid "69af3b77-0084-54dc-ac98-7db1b1663341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336970} {:answer/id #uuid "ded51f56-dcb8-5f7c-824a-7620ec794075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337976} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a084a2-243e-5719-8996-4bd31353ed5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69af3b77-0084-54dc-ac98-7db1b1663341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336970} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0f0b4b5-42cc-570d-8be3-a9eee64f3548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bb88b32-c54c-5495-b159-98b6a3b60727" :question/math-academy-id "q-70200" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as \n$x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441125} {:answer/id #uuid "c159eb9f-4f2c-5439-9834-15476295ce88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441135} {:answer/id #uuid "d56c8d4b-ec4f-5319-9ebf-a207cab9ae06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441137} {:answer/id #uuid "f0696591-4c24-54b6-8b14-e466d380abaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441140} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c1f9ea-b9de-5947-a51a-a2f5c3cb34c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441125} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d79a455-f937-543f-8ebe-441cfa187191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "659100c2-e69a-5015-bd46-ea6499418f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-77396" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447eaab9-6da2-5044-99db-4a1a4223532f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393683} {:answer/id #uuid "78a86f8d-aae4-5a4d-95e4-fab946aebfd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393684} {:answer/id #uuid "38a07045-f8ae-5e87-9321-f64593af7a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393685} {:answer/id #uuid "e48114b7-c325-58ff-8779-f2b138d44c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393686} {:answer/id #uuid "19c2ae1c-bf55-56a8-9095-d30b83511f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a07045-f8ae-5e87-9321-f64593af7a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393685} :answer-field/id #uuid "87423d6e-0ff7-5bbe-8eda-f375b8d4efa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94153e84-a333-5aec-b75c-49c1a118f48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77398" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441124} {:answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} {:answer/id #uuid "45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441129} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441132} {:answer/id #uuid "ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77402" :question/problem "Let $⟨2,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+ky=5 \\\\ x+2y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}]}
